ge issue view 8 -R world/story-repo -c | tail -15 | c…", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/rv && rm -rf sw && git clone -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" sw && cd sw && git log --oneline | head -2; git diff HEAD~1 HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-3500; forge issue view 8 -R world/story-repo -c | tail -15 | cut -c1-2000"]], "output": "```console\ndb746a5 Outline rev 9: one gene_expression account, strongest-valid-baseline rule, clip as claim C8\nb00c5fd Outline rev 8: gene_expression gain is the package lambda clip; two baselines; floor in measured units\n--- a/Outline.md\n+++ b/Outline.md\n-# Outline (story-repo, revision 8 (the gene_expression gain is the package's λ clip; two PPI++ baselines; answers experiment-repo#6); revision 7 (attribution of the gene_expression gain, C3 scoring by bracketed cells, C4 clause refuted at small n; answers idea-review story-repo#7); revision 6 (first results folded in, section 8; headline arm per tier; C3 factor K/(K−1), Brief rev. 7); venue budget applied; answers idea-review #3 in story-repo)\n+# Outline (story-repo, revision 9 (one account of gene_expression; strongest-valid-baseline reading rule; the clip as claim C8, E9; answers idea-review story-repo#8); revision 8 (the gene_expression gain is the package's λ clip; two PPI++ baselines; answers experiment-repo#6); revision 7 (attribution of the gene_expression gain, C3 scoring by bracketed cells, C4 clause refuted at small n; answers idea-review story-repo#7); revision 6 (first results folded in, section 8; headline arm per tier; C3 factor K/(K−1), Brief rev. 7); venue budget applied; answers idea-review #3 in story-repo)\n-| C1 | **Floor + exact gap (setup).** Var of the pooled estimator = Var(Y)/M + (1/n−1/M)Var(Y−g); PPI++ equals the pooled linear estimator; excess over the floor = (1/n−1/M)Δ, Δ = Var(m(f)−a*−b*f); no room iff E[Y\\|f] affine. An algebraic identity: it should pass; refuted only if the synthetic measurements depart from it beyond MC error. | E1 synthetic (Gaussian closed form, sigmoid, non-monotone, affine null), E2 numerical equivalence A2 ≡ pooled linear | Short panel in Fig 3 or appendix figure (predicted vs measured excess), one table line for the equivalence |\n+| C8 | **A condition under which an existing PPI++ interval can be shortened: the λ clip.** The optimal scalar tuning is λ\\* = b·N/M with b = Cov(Y,f)/Var(f); `ppi-python` 0.2.3 clips λ̂ to [0,1], so when λ\\* > 1 (b above about M/N, so b > 1 for N ≫ n) the package interval is wider than the unclipped one. The gain grows with b − 1 and is given by the known variance formula; it is valid only once n is large enough that the unclipped λ̂ is stable. Refuted if, on a synthetic sweep over b, the width gain does not follow the formula, or the gain is absent at b = 1.5 or 2. It is a statement about one implementation, not about the PPI++ method. | E9 synthetic sweep b ∈ {0.8, 1.0, 1.2, 1.5, 2} against the known V formula, n over the grid, N/n as in E3; real sets: b, λ̂ > 1 fraction, ratio vs unclipped (census_income b = 1.38, gene_expression b = 1.15 are the observed cases; the other sets have b < 1) | Fig 6 (gain vs b, synthetic curve with the real sets marked, coverage shown); one paragraph in the text |\n+| C1 | **Floor + exact gap (setup).** Var of the pooled estimator = Var(Y)/M + (1/n−1/M)Var(Y−g); PPI++ with unclipped tuned λ̂ equals the pooled linear estimator (the package's clipped λ̂ does not when b > 1, see C8); excess over the floor = (1/n−1/M)Δ, Δ = Var(m(f)−a*−b*f); no room iff E[Y\\|f] affine. An algebraic identity: it should pass; refuted only if the synthetic measurements depart from it beyond MC error. | E1 synthetic (Gaussian closed form, sigmoid, non-monotone, affine null), E2 numerical equivalence A2 ≡ pooled linear | Short panel in Fig 3 or appendix figure (predicted vs measured excess), one table line for the equivalence |\n+- **E9 The clip (C8).** Synthetic sweep over the slope b with the known variance formula: width of the package PPI++ against unclipped PPI++ (same draws) and the formula, with coverage; on the real sets b, the fraction of draws with λ̂ > 1, and the ratio against unclipped over n. Analysis owns the design.\n+- **Fig 6:** C8 — width gain of unclipped over package PPI++ vs the slope b: synthetic curve and formula, real sets marked, coverage shown.\n-**Venue budget (\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "6ebaf957-7752-5862-a44e-901427559c7d", "at": 1795688847.1803346, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 52272, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "2e912402ccc167304c9998730125edf5", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "e6fce8ab-b2e0-5299-9d76-decec7a021a7", "at": 1795688847.1931493, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 52273, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "2e912402ccc167304c9998730125edf5", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "63a4658a-ea50-502b-89f7-e006ac281098", "at": 1795688847.195403, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 52274, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "2e912402ccc167304c9998730125edf5", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "acc62e4c-9f6f-531d-8dc9-641b2d98ab76", "at": 1795688847.2362676, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 52276, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challeng